  "term": "class inclusion",
  "definition": "In this historical logic usage, class inclusion means understanding a proposition as a relation between classes, where one class falls within or is contained under another. The passage treats this as one way of expressing what a proposition means, paired with and logically equivalent to an attribute-based reading.",
